  "status": "Approved",
  "description": "The proposal is for the construction of a single-story rear extension to the existing dwelling house. The extension will project approximately 6.0 meters from the rear elevation of the property, with a width matching the existing house and a maximum height of approximately 4.0 meters (eaves height approximately 2.6 meters).\n\nThe extension will provide additional internal living space, forming an open-plan kitchen and dining area. The design will be in keeping with the character of the existing property, using matching concrete and roof materials.\n\nFenestration will include rear-facing double doors and rooflights to improve natural light. No changes are proposed to the front elevation of the property.",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The materials used on the external surfaces of the development shall match those used in the building to which it is attached in terms of style, colour, texture and, in the case of brickwork, bonding, coursing and pointing (other than materials used in the construction of a conservatory).\r\nReason: In order to protect the appearance of the area.",
    "Condition : 2 - Any window located in a wall or roof slope forming a side elevation of the dwellinghouse must be: (a) obscure-glazed; and (b) non-opening unless the parts of the window which can be opened are more than 1.7 metres above the floor of the room in which the window is installed. Any such windows shall, once installed, be retained permanently as such, and once built no further side windows shall be installed.\r\nReason: In order to protect neighbours' living conditions."
  ],
